# Fal-X scope denylist.
#
# Entries here override the allowlist, including under --allow-any. Nothing that
# matches is contacted, whatever else says it is reachable.
#
# This is the file most runs will use. It needs no flag: anything listed here is
# skipped by every run.
#
# Use it for the things that are technically in scope but that you do not want
# touched: a staging environment under development, a domain that hands over to
# a third party, a range that belongs to someone else.
#
# Same syntax as the allowlist. `fal-x install --setup` writes a copy to
# config/out-of-scope.txt, which is read automatically. --exclude points at a
# different file for one run.
